  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multi-profile with scVI n200 + transformer aggregation is the current best (0.653), and image-only ResNet50 is very weak (0.208). The key uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion can add any complementary signal on top of the strong RNA multi-profile baseline, or whether the weak image modality will dilute performance. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multi-profile, scVI n200, ResNet50, transformer, concat) directly tests whether the best RNA configuration benefits from adding image features via simple concatenation. It is the most logical single extension of the current best setup, changes only the model setting (adding image + fusion) while keeping all other choices at their validated optima. If it fails to beat 0.653, we can confidently conclude image adds no value and spend remaining budget on RNA-only refinements; if it succeeds, it opens a productive multimodal direction for the final 3 experiments."
}

